            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35692"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35693</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>dicarboxylic acid anion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35701 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35701">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_36963"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A compound formally derived from an oxoacid R&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;k&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;E(=O)&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;l&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;(OH)&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;m&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; (&lt;em&gt;l&lt;/em&gt; &gt; 0) and an alcohol, phenol, heteroarenol, or enol by linking with formal loss of water from an acidic hydroxy group of the former and a hydroxy group of the latter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35701</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>ester</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35703 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35703">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24432"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A xenobiotic (Greek, &lt;em&gt;xenos&lt;/em&gt; &quot;foreign&quot;; &lt;em&gt;bios&lt;/em&gt; &quot;life&quot;) is a compound that is foreign to a living organism. Principal xenobiotics include: drugs, carcinogens and various compounds that have been introduced into the environment by artificial means.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35703</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>xenobiotic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50846"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An agent that suppresses immune function by one of several mechanisms of action. Classical cytotoxic immunosuppressants act by inhibiting DNA synthesis. Others may act through activation of T-cells or by inhibiting the activation of helper cells. In addition, an immunosuppressive agent is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to diminish the extent and/or voracity of an immune response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35705</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>immunosuppressive agent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35715 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35715">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_51143"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_29785"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A compound having a nitro group, ‒NO&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; (free valence on nitrogen), which may be attached to carbon, nitrogen (as in nitramines), or oxygen (as in nitrates), among other elements (in the absence of specification, &lt;em&gt;C&lt;/em&gt;-nitro compounds are usually implied).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35715</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>nitro compound</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35716 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35716">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35715"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_72695"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018036"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_136622"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nitro compound having the nitro group (‒NO&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;) attached to a carbon atom.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35716</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>C-nitro compound</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35717 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35717">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35488"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A central nervous system depressant used to induce drowsiness or sleep or to reduce psychological excitement or anxiety.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35717</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>sedative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35718 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35718">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33281"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An  antimicrobial agent that destroys fungi by suppressing their ability to grow or reproduce.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35718</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal agent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35725 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35725">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33308"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018038"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17824"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any carboxylic ester resulting from the formal condensation of a carboxylic acid with the hydroxy group of propan-2-ol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35725</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>isopropyl ester</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35748 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35748">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33308"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_61697"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A carboxylic ester in which the carboxylic acid component can be any fatty acid.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35748</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fatty acid ester</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35757 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35757">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_29067"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_25384"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A carboxylic acid anion formed when the carboxy group of a monocarboxylic acid is deprotonated.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:35757</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>monocarboxylic acid anion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35788 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35788">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35341"/>
