        <obo:IAO_0000115>A compound in which monosaccharide units are joined by glycosidic linkages. The term is commonly used to refer to a defined structure as opposed to a polymer of unspecified length or a homologous mixture. When the linkages are of other types the compounds are regarded as oligosaccharide analogues.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>CHEBI:50699</oboInOwl:id>
