    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000933 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000933">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000929"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000938"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_66901"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000938"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000108"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>CYP107S1 is a cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzyme found in the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It can metabolize fluoroquinolone antibiotics (ciprofloxacin and fleroxacin), a cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator potentiator (ivacaftor), and a selective estrogen receptor modulator antimicrobial adjuvant (raloxifene).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dcterms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>HMDM:0000933</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Pseudomonas aeruginosa CYP107S1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000933"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CYP107S1 is a cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzyme found in the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It can metabolize fluoroquinolone antibiotics (ciprofloxacin and fleroxacin), a cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator potentiator (ivacaftor), and a selective estrogen receptor modulator antimicrobial adjuvant (raloxifene).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39032655</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000934 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000934">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000073"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The CFTR potentiators increase channel activity of the CFRT protein located at the cell surface and enhance ion transport. Ivacaftor is the first intervention that corrects the underlying molecular defect in CF. It has demonstrated effectiveness in people with a class III mutation (G551D) and some effectiveness with class IV mutations (R117H) and has the potential to be used for other class III and IV mutations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dcterms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>HMDM:0000934</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) potentiators</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000934"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The CFTR potentiators increase channel activity of the CFRT protein located at the cell surface and enhance ion transport. Ivacaftor is the first intervention that corrects the underlying molecular defect in CF. It has demonstrated effectiveness in people with a class III mutation (G551D) and some effectiveness with class IV mutations (R117H) and has the potential to be used for other class III and IV mutations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25811419</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30616300</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000937 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000937">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000012"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This family of enzymes use molybdopterin as a cofactor to catalyze various redox reactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dcterms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>HMDM:0000937</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>molybdopterin-containing oxidoreductase family</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


